490 0 obj
<</E(As you can imagine, the GKS scholarship is highly competitive. The same goes for the other scholarships we saw here. You will be competing against excellent students throughout the world for a limited number of places. But do not let it intimidate you because it is very much possible. Hard, but possible. I know because I got admitted to the best STEM university and received one of these scholarships.)/K[ 25]/P 147 0 R /Pg 24 0 R /S/P/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
491 0 obj
<</E(Now, I would like to offer specific advice on how you can improve your chances of getting admitted in Korean universities and winning massive scholarships like the GKS.)/K[ 26]/P 147 0 R /Pg 24 0 R /S/P/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
492 0 obj
<</E(Advice to Win Admissions and Scholarships)/K[ 0]/P 148 0 R /Pg 25 0 R /S/H1/T(Advice to Win Admissions and Scholarships)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
493 0 obj
<</E(The Six Pillars of a Strong Application)/K[ 1]/P 148 0 R /Pg 25 0 R /S/H2/T(The Six Pillars of a Strong Application)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
494 0 obj
<</E(Korean universities generally do not disclose the details of their admission process. Plus, I have never served on an admission committee. So, I do not have official information about how exactly applications are evaluated.)/K[ 2]/P 148 0 R /Pg 25 0 R /S/P/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
495 0 obj
<</E(That said, based on my own experience as a successful applicant, conversations with other successful applicants, my understanding of Korean academic culture and institutions, and my experience advising prospective students, I believe that I can offer sensible advice in this topic.)/K[ 3]/P 148 0 R /Pg 25 0 R /S/P/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
496 0 obj
<</E(The advice here is written with South Korea in mind. But I believe that it also largely applies to culturally close countries such as China and Japan.)/K[ 4]/P 148 0 R /Pg 25 0 R /S/P/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
497 0 obj
<</E(Academic Excellence)/K[ 5]/P 148 0 R /Pg 25 0 R /S/H2/T(Academic Excellence)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
498 0 obj
<</E(In South Korea, you will primarily be judged on your academic performance. I have noticed that academic achievement is consistently listed as the first evaluation criterion in admission guides.)/K[ 6]/P 148 0 R /Pg 25 0 R /S/P/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
499 0 obj
<</E(If you are targeting Tier 1 universities and full scholarships in particular, academic excellence is non-negotiable. This does not mean getting perfect grades, it means demonstrating a consistently high level of academic achievement to convince universities of your academic potential. It seems to me that South Korean universities tend to place a much greater emphasis on academic performance than institutions in Western countries like the US or Canada. It is given more weight in the evaluation process, especially compared to non-academic extracurricular activities such as sports or volunteering.)/K[ 7]/P 148 0 R /Pg 25 0 R /S/P/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
500 0 obj
<</E<>/K[ 8]/P 148 0 R /Pg 25 0 R /S/P/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
501 0 obj
<</E<>/K[ 0]/P 149 0 R /Pg 26 0 R /S/P/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
502 0 obj
<</E(Proofs of Interest)/K[ 1]/P 149 0 R /Pg 26 0 R /S/H1/T(Proofs of Interest)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
503 0 obj
<</E(The second most important element, in my view, is what I call proofs of interest. These are activities, projects, and achievements that prove that you are genuinely interested in your desired major.)/K[ 2]/P 149 0 R /Pg 26 0 R /S/P/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
504 0 obj
<</E(For example, suppose that you claim to be interested in computer science. Well, what have you done with that interest? What do you have to show for that interest? We need to know otherwise your application risk being too light or appearing inauthentic. You might start or engage in a computer science club, teach programming to your classmates, build useful programs that have some impact \(even a minimal local impact\), or compete in CS competitions. See, the objective is to show that your interest is so strong that it forces you to take action.)/K[ 3]/P 149 0 R /Pg 26 0 R /S/P/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
505 0 obj
<</E(Personally, I am interested in mathematics. In my application, I talked about my endeavor to extend the concept of the power of a point into three dimensions, as well as other mathematical explorations like a function to detect prime numbers and an ordering relation in a plane. I also participated and received awards in several international and national mathematics competitions. These are activities and achievements that prove better than words ever could that I am truly passionate about mathematics.)/K[ 4]/P 149 0 R /Pg 26 0 R /S/P/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
506 0 obj
<</E(Korean universities will ask you directly or indirectly for proofs of interest. For instance, consider the personal statement prompts used by Sungkyunkwan University for the Fall 2027 application:)/K[ 5]/P 149 0 R /Pg 26 0 R /S/P/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
507 0 obj
<</E(   Please describe any academic achievements or activities related to areas of interest that you pursued during your high school years, along with the outcomes.)/K[ 6]/P 909 0 R /Pg 26 0 R /S/P/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
508 0 obj
<</E(   Please explain in detail your preparation and efforts for studying abroad in Korea.)/K[ 7]/P 910 0 R /Pg 26 0 R /S/P/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
509 0 obj
<</E(   Please describe up to three activities related to the admission unit you are applying for that you pursued with commitment and significance during your high school years.)/K[ 8]/P 911 0 R /Pg 26 0 R /S/P/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
510 0 obj
<</E(These three essay prompts are essentially asking the following question:)/K[ 9]/P 149 0 R /Pg 26 0 R /S/P/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
511 0 obj
<</E<8D576861742070726F766573207468617420796F7520617265207265616C6C7920696E746572657374656420696E20796F75722063686F73656E206669656C64206F7220696E207374756479696E6720696E204B6F7265613F8E>/K[ 10]/P 149 0 R /Pg 26 0 R /S/H1/T<8D576861742070726F766573207468617420796F7520617265207265616C6C7920696E746572657374656420696E20796F75722063686F73656E206669656C64206F7220696E207374756479696E6720696E204B6F7265613F8E>/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
512 0 obj
<</E(The same pattern can be found in KAIST and POSTECH application essays. When writing such essays, I believe substance matters more than style, although both are important. An essay with simple words and sentence structures built around compelling evidence of genuine interest will perform better than an elegantly written essay filled with empty words.)/K[ 11]/P 149 0 R /Pg 26 0 R /S/P/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
513 0 obj
<</E(It is my belief that proofs of interest constitute such a strong element of your application that in some cases they may compensate for academic results that are good but not exceptional. In my opinion, an applicant with 35/45 in the IB and outstanding proofs of interest is not necessarily less competitive than an applicant with 39/45 in the IB with common extracurricular activities that are unrelated to their field of study. So even though academic excellence remains the number one criterion, proofs of interest are a very close second. Therefore, build, create, explore, collaborate, compete, teach, and engage with the subjects that genuinely interest you.)/K[ 12]/P 149 0 R /Pg 26 0 R /S/P/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
514 0 obj
<</E(You will be the first beneficiary of these efforts. Doing activities in fields you are interested in should bring you joy, create wonderful memories, and contribute to your personal growth. In addition, it will help you test your true level of interest. These benefits remain valuable regardless of the outcome of any university or scholarship application.)/K[ 0]/P 150 0 R /Pg 27 0 R /S/H3/T(You will be the first beneficiary of these efforts. Doing activities in fields you are interested in should bring you joy, create wonderful memories, and contribute to your personal growth. In addition, it will help you test your true level of interest. These benefits remain valuable regardless of the outcome of any university or scholarship application.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
515 0 obj
<</E(Awards and Recognition)/K[ 1]/P 150 0 R /Pg 27 0 R /S/H2/T(Awards and Recognition)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
516 0 obj
<</E(The third most important element of an application is awards and recognition. This includes honors, trophies, distinctions, certificates, and other forms of recognition that you typically earn at competitions.)/K[ 2]/P 150 0 R /Pg 27 0 R /S/H3/T(The third most important element of an application is awards and recognition. This includes honors, trophies, distinctions, certificates, and other forms of recognition that you typically earn at competitions.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
517 0 obj
<</E(Many Korean universities, especially Tier 1 universities, are looking for students who stand out from their peers. Being recognized as the best or among the best at something helps in that regard. So, participate in local, national, and international competitions whenever possible. If these competitions align with your field of interest, it is even better.)/K[ 3]/P 150 0 R /Pg 27 0 R /S/H3/T(Many Korean universities, especially Tier 1 universities, are looking for students who stand out from their peers. Being recognized as the best or among the best at something helps in that regard. So, participate in local, national, and international competitions whenever possible. If these competitions align with your field of interest, it is even better.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
518 0 obj
<</E(In my case, I was a finalist in the International Youth Math Challenge, where I received the Bronze Honor. I also participated in the Breakthrough Junior Challenge, a prestigious global science contest. I did not win this one but the experience was valuable. And that is something I want you to understand: you do not have to win every competition you enter. Participating itself demonstrates that you are not afraid of taking initiative, putting yourself out there and challenging yourself. These are qualities that many universities are looking for.)/K[ 4]/P 150 0 R /Pg 27 0 R /S/H3/T(In my case, I was a finalist in the International Youth Math Challenge, where I received the Bronze Honor. I also participated in the Breakthrough Junior Challenge, a prestigious global science contest. I did not win this one but the experience was valuable. And that is something I want you to understand: you do not have to win every competition you enter. Participating itself demonstrates that you are not afraid of taking initiative, putting yourself out there and challenging yourself. These are qualities that many universities are looking for.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
519 0 obj
<</E(Note that awards and recognition are also closely connected to the first two pillars. An academic award from your school serves as evidence of academic excellence, while a prize \(even a participation certificate\) in a physics competition constitutes a proof of interest in that field.)/K[ 5]/P 150 0 R /Pg 27 0 R /S/H3/T(Note that awards and recognition are also closely connected to the first two pillars. An academic award from your school serves as evidence of academic excellence, while a prize \(even a participation certificate\) in a physics competition constitutes a proof of interest in that field.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
520 0 obj
<</E<>/K[ 6]/P 150 0 R /Pg 27 0 R /S/H3/T<>/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
521 0 obj
<</E(So again, I encourage you to seek out competitive opportunities in your areas of interest. Whether you win or not, the experience will help you grow and demonstrate qualities and abilities that universities value.)/K[ 7]/P 150 0 R /Pg 27 0 R /S/H3/T(So again, I encourage you to seek out competitive opportunities in your areas of interest. Whether you win or not, the experience will help you grow and demonstrate qualities and abilities that universities value.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
522 0 obj
<</E(Authenticity)/K[ 8]/P 150 0 R /Pg 27 0 R /S/H1/T(Authenticity)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
523 0 obj
<</E(My fourth piece of advice is to present an authentic story.)/K[ 9]/P 150 0 R /Pg 27 0 R /S/H3/T(My fourth piece of advice is to present an authentic story.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
524 0 obj
<</E<>/K[ 10]/P 150 0 R /Pg 27 0 R /S/H3/T<>/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
525 0 obj
<</E(Be yourself. Do not lie in your application. You do not need to lie, because you are enough, you are deserving. So be truthful and let your true soul speak in your essays.)/K[ 11]/P 150 0 R /Pg 27 0 R /S/H3/T(Be yourself. Do not lie in your application. You do not need to lie, because you are enough, you are deserving. So be truthful and let your true soul speak in your essays.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
526 0 obj
<</E(For example, do not be afraid to discuss mistakes or setbacks and how you grew from them. I did the same at the time I applied. I wrote about how I was in a very deplorable situation due to my own doing. I explained how I had to reassess myself to grow out of it. I could have written about a time where I was brave and heroic \(I had many stories like that\), but I chose to be vulnerable and real. Now, I was not part of the admission committee, but I believe that it earned me good points.)/K[ 0]/P 151 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S/H2/T(For example, do not be afraid to discuss mistakes or setbacks and how you grew from them. I did the same at the time I applied. I wrote about how I was in a very deplorable situation due to my own doing. I explained how I had to reassess myself to grow out of it. I could have written about a time where I was brave and heroic \(I had many stories like that\), but I chose to be vulnerable and real. Now, I was not part of the admission committee, but I believe that it earned me good points.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
527 0 obj
<</E(Besides, admission officers have read thousands of application essays already. They can detect fakeness and disingenuity, and that will not work in your favor. So, remain authentic. Be yourself.)/K[ 1]/P 151 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S/H2/T(Besides, admission officers have read thousands of application essays already. They can detect fakeness and disingenuity, and that will not work in your favor. So, remain authentic. Be yourself.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
528 0 obj
<</E(Vision)/K[ 2]/P 151 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S/H1/T(Vision)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
529 0 obj
<</E(The fifth pillar of a strong application is a strong vision.)/K[ 3]/P 151 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S/H2/T(The fifth pillar of a strong application is a strong vision.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
530 0 obj
<</E(What do you want to study? Why? What are you aiming at in life? Why have you chosen South Korea, and this particular university? How does it all tie to what you want to study and do in life? We should have a good idea of where you are going and why.)/K[ 4]/P 151 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S/H2/T(What do you want to study? Why? What are you aiming at in life? Why have you chosen South Korea, and this particular university? How does it all tie to what you want to study and do in life? We should have a good idea of where you are going and why.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
531 0 obj
<</E(Now, you are still in high school. Nobody expects you to have figured out everything at your age. You still have many doubts and hesitations, and you likely have misconceptions about many important things. But at the very least, you should have some sense of direction, even if it may change later. Admission officers should feel that you are not going to university just because that is what naturally comes after high school, but because your purpose leads you there.)/K[ 5]/P 151 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S/H2/T(Now, you are still in high school. Nobody expects you to have figured out everything at your age. You still have many doubts and hesitations, and you likely have misconceptions about many important things. But at the very least, you should have some sense of direction, even if it may change later. Admission officers should feel that you are not going to university just because that is what naturally comes after high school, but because your purpose leads you there.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
532 0 obj
<</E<>/K[ 6]/P 151 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S/H2/T<>/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
533 0 obj
<</E<>/K[ 7]/P 151 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S/H2/T<>/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
534 0 obj
<</E(Note that proofs of interest can help you show that your vision is not just an empty declaration.)/K[ 8]/P 151 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S/H2/T(Note that proofs of interest can help you show that your vision is not just an empty declaration.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
535 0 obj
<</E(Language)/K[ 9]/P 151 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S/H1/T(Language)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
536 0 obj
<</E(Finally, the sixth and final pillar is language proficiency.)/K[ 10]/P 151 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S/H2/T(Finally, the sixth and final pillar is language proficiency.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
537 0 obj
<</E(First of all, English is obviously non-negotiable for English-taught programs. You should be able to follow a course entirely delivered in English, and you will have to prove this to your university. Each university will tell you the proof of English proficiency that it accepts. Some universities require TOEFL or IELTS, while others like KAIST may waive this requirement for students who have studied at an English-medium institution. You will have to check the English language requirements of each university you are interested in.)/K[ 11]/P 151 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S/H2/T(First of all, English is obviously non-negotiable for English-taught programs. You should be able to follow a course entirely delivered in English, and you will have to prove this to your university. Each university will tell you the proof of English proficiency that it accepts. Some universities require TOEFL or IELTS, while others like KAIST may waive this requirement for students who have studied at an English-medium institution. You will have to check the English language requirements of each university you are interested in.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
538 0 obj
<</E<>/K[ 0]/P 152 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S/H2/T<>/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
539 0 obj
<</E<>/K[ 1]/P 152 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S/H2/T<>/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
540 0 obj
<</E(Now, learning a language is time-consuming. You can absolutely get into a good university with good scholarship without knowing Korean. I for one did not know a single word of Korean when I was admitted. My point is simply that, for someone who is really serious and determined to study in Korea, having some proficiency in Korean can make a positive difference in their application.)/K[ 2]/P 152 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S/H2/T(Now, learning a language is time-consuming. You can absolutely get into a good university with good scholarship without knowing Korean. I for one did not know a single word of Korean when I was admitted. My point is simply that, for someone who is really serious and determined to study in Korea, having some proficiency in Korean can make a positive difference in their application.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
541 0 obj
<</E(Final Thoughts)/K[ 3]/P 152 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S/H1/T(Final Thoughts)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
542 0 obj
<</E(These are my six most important pieces of advice for building a strong application to the best universities and scholarships in South Korea. They helped me gain admission to KAIST, and they also helped other Cameroonian and foreign students I have supported with their applications to Korean universities. So, the advice here can definitely help you too. I am sharing these with you because I genuinely believe that you have what it takes to seize the best higher education opportunities in South Korea.)/K[ 4]/P 152 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S/H2/T(These are my six most important pieces of advice for building a strong application to the best universities and scholarships in South Korea. They helped me gain admission to KAIST, and they also helped other Cameroonian and foreign students I have supported with their applications to Korean universities. So, the advice here can definitely help you too. I am sharing these with you because I genuinely believe that you have what it takes to seize the best higher education opportunities in South Korea.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
